<title>USA: Novartis expanding U.S. hybrid seed sales.</title>
<headline>Novartis expanding U.S. hybrid seed sales.</headline>
<dateline>GOLDEN VALLEY, Minn. 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Novartis Seeds Inc said Wednesday it received regulatory approval to expand the sales range of its NK Brand Bt corn hybrids in the United States.</p>
<p>The move by the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency allows Novartis to market the Bt hybrid corn seeds to growers in the South for the first time. A previous registration allowed sales of Bt corn hybrids in the rest of the country, Novartis Seeds said.</p>
<p>Novartis Seeds is an affiliate of Novartis Seeds AG of Switzerland.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
